    "scope": "Complete supported resource membership and exact byte equality bind independently prepared basis/target roots through the checked journal. Complete-target recovery adds immutable action evidence. Terminal cleanup and explicit audited orphan takeover retain exact target bytes across real process stops and lost durability responses. First-receipt creation/write/synchronization failures report possible operational mutation without claiming a normative write or completion. Operational directory, receipt, marker and terminal audit effects stay attributed to the current invocation; read-only conflicts do not imply its mutation. Bound rollback copies, cursor/terminal journals, completion receipts/marker and action/rollback receipts are published only after complete staging. Initial allocation/write failures expose no short canonical helper. Tested repeated native failures and real process stops remain explicitly resumable; foreign or altered bindings block publication, existing evidence retains its bytes and original authority, and mutation diagnostics retain possible operational changes. No automatic recovery, comprehensive fault-injection or restore acceptance."
